    "body": "## Context\n\nKeycast PR #235 (account suspension) merged May 20. Keycast now exposes `GET/PUT /api/admin/users/:pubkey/status` with service-token auth. Status values: `active`, `suspended`, `banned`. Suspended users cannot sign events or decrypt DMs via the signer.\n\nRelay-manager's age review system currently restricts accounts by age-restricting media (Blossom) and optionally banning the pubkey (Funnelcake). This is effective but imprecise: media restriction hides existing content, but the user can still post new events via any client that doesn't use Keycast signing. With Keycast suspension, the restriction is authoritative.\n\n## What\n\nWhen a moderator transitions an age review case to a restricted state (`restricted_pending_user_response`, `restricted_pending_support_email`):\n- Call `PUT /api/admin/users/:pubkey/status` with `{ status: \"suspended\", suspended_reason: \"age_review\" }`\n\nWhen a moderator clears the case (`clear`):\n- Call `PUT /api/admin/users/:pubkey/status` with `{ status: \"active\" }`\n\nWhen a case expires (cron auto-close with deny outcome):\n- Keep suspended (no unsuspend call)\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- `KEYCAST_SERVICE_TOKEN` secret set on relay-manager staging + production\n- `KEYCAST_URL` env var (probably `https://login.divine.video`)\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Restricting an account in age review suspends the user in Keycast\n- Clearing a case unsuspends the user in Keycast\n- Keycast call failure does not block the age review state transition (graceful degradation -- log the error, continue)\n- Integration test covering the suspend/unsuspend calls\n\n## Related\n\n- Keycast PR divinevideo/keycast#235 (merged)\n- Relay-manager PR #78 (deletion alignment, in review)\n- Under-16 coordination doc: `docs/moderation/under-16-system-coordination.md`",
